# Category files

## Summary

A category's files, under the media collection `categories`: staff with the `update` permission upload images, change their details and remove them.

## Requirements

- **CATFILES** — A category takes PNG, JPG, JPEG and SVG files, under the media types of the `categories` collection.
- **FILESLOCK** — Where `showPublic` is set, the files of a category of an organisation outside the organisation tree can't be added, changed or removed, except by a super admin of categories.
- **FILESDONE** — An added file shows "Image was added" and a changed one "Media was updated"; a failure shows the backend's error, or "Saving failed" when it gives none.

## Tests

- Uploading a PDF to a category is refused by the file picker.
- With `showPublic`, a staff member sees no add, edit or delete buttons on the files of another organisation's category outside their tree.

## View: CategoryMedia

### Summary

The Media tab of an opened category.

### Display

- The category's files with their title and media type; images and videos previewed, other files downloaded — [reads](aim:juicebar.categories#Record:Category), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIALIST])
- No add, edit or delete buttons where the files are locked — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.media#Requirements[FILESLOCK]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories#Requirements[ORGTREE])

### Actions

- Add — [exposes](aim:juicebar.categories.media#Operation:AddCategoryFile)
- Edit — [exposes](aim:juicebar.categories.media#Operation:UpdateCategoryFile)
- Delete — [exposes](aim:juicebar.categories.media#Operation:RemoveCategoryFile)

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/categories/details/category-media/category-media.component.ts#CategoryMediaComponent` — as: component
- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/shared/components/media/media.component.ts#MediaComponent` — as: component
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: AddCategoryFile

### Summary

A staff member uploads a file to a category under one of the collection's media types.

### Input

```schema
categoryId: string required ref(juicebar.categories#Category.id)
mediaTypeKey: string required
file: file required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.categories#Persona:CategoryEditor`
- `juicebar.categories#Persona:CategorySuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The file is kept in the file store under the category and added to the category's files — [invokes](aim:juicebar#Capability:MediaStorage), [mutates](aim:juicebar.categories#Record:Category), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.media#Requirements[CATFILES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIATYPES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIASIZE])
- A notice tells whether it worked — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.media#Requirements[FILESDONE])
- The operation is refused without the `update` permission, or for a category of another organisation — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories#Requirements[CATROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories#Requirements[CATORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/categories/details/category-media/category-media.component.ts#CategoryMediaComponent.added` — as: component
- binds: `service:juicecommerce:categories#addMedia` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: UpdateCategoryFile

### Summary

A staff member changes a file's details: its name, title, description, alternative text and media type.

### Input

```schema
categoryId: string required ref(juicebar.categories#Category.id)
mediaId: string required
key: string
mediaType: map(string)
name: map(string)
title: map(string)
description: map(string)
alt_text: map(string)
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.categories#Persona:CategoryEditor`
- `juicebar.categories#Persona:CategorySuperAdmin`

### Ensures

- The file's details are replaced with the ones given — [mutates](aim:juicebar.categories#Record:Category), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIALIST])
- A notice tells whether it worked — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories.media#Requirements[FILESDONE])
- The operation is refused without the `update` permission, or for a category of another organisation — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories#Requirements[CATROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories#Requirements[CATORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/categories/details/category-media/category-media.component.ts#CategoryMediaComponent.updated` — as: component
- binds: `service:juicecommerce:categories#updateMedia` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred

## Operation: RemoveCategoryFile

### Summary

A staff member removes a file from a category.

### Input

```schema
categoryId: string required ref(juicebar.categories#Category.id)
mediaId: string required
```

### Authz

- `juicebar.categories#Persona:CategoryEditor`
- `juicebar.categories#Persona:CategorySuperAdmin`

### Expects

- The staff member confirmed the removal.

### Ensures

- The file is no longer among the category's files — [mutates](aim:juicebar.categories#Record:Category), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.core#Requirements[MEDIALIST])
- The operation is refused without the `update` permission, or for a category of another organisation — [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories#Requirements[CATROLE]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]), [satisfies](aim:juicebar.categories#Requirements[CATORG])

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/categories/details/category-media/category-media.component.ts#CategoryMediaComponent.removed` — as: component
- binds: `service:juicecommerce:categories#removeMedia` — as: handler
- provenance: inferred
